&lt;/div&gt;



&lt;p&gt;Notice &lt;code&gt;customWastePercent&lt;/code&gt; — an optional override with &lt;code&gt;??&lt;/code&gt;, not &lt;code&gt;||&lt;/code&gt;. If someone explicitly wants &lt;code&gt;0%&lt;/code&gt; waste for a test calculation, &lt;code&gt;||&lt;/code&gt; would silently fall back to the pattern default because &lt;code&gt;0&lt;/code&gt; is falsy. That's the kind of bug that only surfaces in a code review months later when someone asks "why can't I set waste to zero?"&lt;/p&gt;




